eamed replay where they have separate wiring; independently remove or bypass each relevant ceiling to show the tests fail. Use bounded malformed fixtures, not an allocation bomb or a noisy RSS threshold. Preserve authentication before decompression, fail-closed fallback, sequence/tree binding, current cache formats, and existing supported read/write behavior. The old attachment-count mismatch is already fixed and is outside this recovery.\n\nReconcile current source bases and addressee availability with Planner before starting if the queued request is stale. Keep #21351's distinct signed causal-trailer equality repair separate and preserve its resulting tests. Publish the exact implementation head and reporting artifact; obtain independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review; merge the approved head with exact-path succession, push, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch. Do not report the historical mutation as a current result or claim a new memory/security guarantee from this test cleanup.","body":{"branch":"request/checkpoint-decoder-regression","conditions":"Remove the weaker parallel compact-checkpoint test decoder through production-path fixtures; mutation-sensitive bounded preallocation and aggregate-ceiling tests on real compact/streamed paths; preserve signatures, fallback, compatibility and existing limits; exact-head independent review, sealed delivery, push, CI and worktree cleanup. Historical mutation is evidence to refresh, not a claimed current test result.","head":"5cc098a8ecf9e7c460c08a458ed2baa069d7803b","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4c4f0d4142bfa057005b09e59bc0a3462980842b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:79e90bb8d9471285ac5b07040a923a9352610ccb stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a371f3378a44dbcfed4d24deb224d8c76a9667e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:191ece9ae6bdc7636c4bc5c219e6af3a